Bootstrap Chain Milestones
==========================

Version  Milestone
-------  ---------
00       Minimal DATA-only bootstrap (129 bytes)
01       First non-standard 6502 mnemonics
02       Source becomes human-readable assembly
03       Byte selectors, label assignments, origin setting
05       Two-pass assembly (forward references)
07       Instruction table generator (instgen)
10       .include directive
11       First modularized source
16       Standard 6502 syntax support
17       Source transitions to standard syntax
18       Forward reference tracking
19       Expression evaluation
20       .ifdef/.endif conditional assembly
22       Macros
23       Self-hosting, .ifndef/.else


Source Syntax Evolution
=======================
Each version's source code can only use syntax supported by the assembler
that builds it. This table shows when new syntax first appears in source.

Version  New syntax used in source
-------  -------------------------
01       None (still DATA hex bytes, assembled by v00)
02       Non-standard mnemonics, labels, label references
03       Character escape literals in operands
04       Label assignments (=), < > byte selectors
05       * = origin directive
06       None
07       None
08       Zero page addressing without < prefix
09       None
10       None
11       .include directive
12       None
13       .zeropage and .code directives
14       None
15       Local labels (.prefix)
16       None
17       Standard 6502 syntax, #'x' character literals
18       None
19       .data directive (replaces DATA)
20       Expression evaluation (+, -), character literal arithmetic
21       .ifdef/.endif, define: command line
22       Label colons, macros, << >> operators
23       .byte, .word, .asciiz, decimal constants
